1	1	what is a scalar quanity and give me exmaples	\N	Physics	Physical Quantities and Units (Scalar and Vector Quantities)	A scalar quantity has magnitude only and no direction. Examples include:\n\n| Scalar Quantity | SI Unit         |\n|----------------|-----------------|\n| Distance       | metre ($m$)     |\n| Speed          | metre/second ($m/s$) |\n| Mass           | kilogram ($kg$) |\n| Time           | second ($s$)    |\n| Temperature    | kelvin ($K$)    |\n| Energy         | joule ($J$)     |\n| Volume         | cubic metre ($m^3$) |\n	[{"step_number": 1, "description": "Define scalar quantity.", "formula": "", "explanation": "A scalar quantity is described completely by its magnitude (size or numerical value) alone, without any reference to direction."}, {"step_number": 2, "description": "List examples of scalar quantities.", "formula": "", "explanation": "Common examples of scalar quantities found in physics are shown in the table below:"}, {"step_number": 3, "description": "Present examples in a table format.", "formula": "", "explanation": "See the table below for examples."}]	["Vector Quantities", "Physical Quantities and Units", "Measurement"]	2026-01-14 12:39:33.58914+01
